As a wizard, your ac is most likely going to be relatively high for a
while. Studded leather is a good choice for armor, and things like
leather gloves, leather helms, etc can add a few extra points. If you
go for dagger throwing, though (not a bad idea, since Magicbane uses
dagger skill), grab the first set of mithril armor you find... casting
will suck, but you will be much more survivable.

> I've tried writing E-word into dust, but many times monsters seem to
> ignore it. One hit is often too much when your HP is 15 and AC 7...
> Engraving E-word takes too long, and I don't always have hard ring or
> gem to write with. Anyways I would prefer not to use Elbereth too much.

They don't ignore it, but you only have about a 72% chance of writing
it in the dust correctly (1/25 chance of messing up each letter, but
you can use : to check this), and attacking or throwing things also
rubs it out. With some experience you can learn to fight fairly
effectively while standing on dusted e squares (hint: write it many
times), but generally it's better to just use it to give yourself a
breather.

Hope that helps,
